===== pm commit --help
usage: pm commit [-h] -m MESSAGE [PATH ...]

Commit only the named records, so other sessions' uncommitted edits in the shared store are left alone. With no path, it lists what is uncommitted and commits nothing. A record uses only these fenced blocks: ::: decision, ::: result and ```mermaid; put a one-line reading under each diagram or large table. An image file (.svg, .png, .jpg, .webp) beside a record is named and committed like one; the site serves it next to the record's page.

positional arguments:
  PATH                  a record you edited: records/<…>.md, a path in the store, relative to it from inside it, or relative to the store from anywhere (sprints/<…>.md)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -m, --message MESSAGE
                        what the hand edit changed
